eeds jolt.io-poller's readiness\n                           backend (kqueue, epoll or WSAPoll); throws on a\n                           platform without one.\n    :worker-threads        worker pool size (threads strategy)\n                            (default = available processors); slow or idle\n                            keep-alive connections occupy a worker each,\n                            but under accept pressure keep-alive is declined\n                            (Connection: close) so queued connections never\n                            starve\n    :keep-alive-timeout-ms idle keep-alive timeout (default 30000)\n    :handler-timeout-ms    how long one handler call may take (default 0 =\n                           no deadline). Past it the request is answered\n                           through :on-failure, then a plain 503, and the\n                           worker goes back to serving; the abandoned\n                           handler's thread is not reclaimed. Costs a thread\n                           handoff per request under :threads (~15-25%\n                           throughput), nothing under :fibers\n    :handler-on-fiber      run the handler on the connection's fiber instead of\n                           handing it to a thread (default false; :fibers only,\n                           and not with :handler-timeout-ms, since a deadline\n                           needs a thread to walk away from). Saves two thread\n                           wakes per request. A handler that blocks somewhere\n                           the runtime cannot see holds its carrier and every\n                           fiber on it: see the README\n    :tls                   {:cert-file :key-file}, both PEM paths, to serve HTTPS\n                           (and wss) on this port, with either strategy.\n                           :cert-file may hold the whole chain, leaf first.\n                           TLS 1.2 or newer. Throws here on a file that is\n                           missing or a key that does not match. Needs OpenSSL,\n                           loaded only when this is set\n    :reuse-port            bind with SO_REUSEPORT (default false), so several\n                           processes can share the port and the kernel spreads\n                           connections over them (Linux)\n    :max-request-bytes     request cap (default 1048576; 413/431 beyond)\n    :ws-handler            fn of a ring-chez.websocket Session, run when a\n                           websocket upgrade request arrives. The session's\n                           :request is the upgrade request." _kc$2131 1139 _kc$2132 1 _kc$2133 "ring_chez/adapter.clj")))))) _kc$2134))) (jolt-register-source! "run-server" "ring-chez.adapter" "run-server" "ring_chez/adapter.clj" 1139) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 0 "static-member" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1133 "$Rnot" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1133 "map?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1134 "ex-info" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1136 "require" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1137 "resolve" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1192 "get" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1193 "$Rnot" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1193 "contains?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1194 "ex-info" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1196 "$R=" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1196 "$Rnot" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1197 "ex-info" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1197 "str" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1200 "validate-opts!" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1202 "$R=" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1202 "$Rnot" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1203 "ex-info" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1205 "pos?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1206 "ex-info" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "run-server" 1206 "str" #f) (jolt-register-callsi